<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/South-Fields.jpg" alt="Plein air painting of the south fields at Ayrshire Farm in Upperville VA" width="450" height="338" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Ayrshire Farm South Field (plein air). 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Today we finally got the opportunity to paint at Ayrshire Farm in Upperville, VA. The farm is about 800 acres in size (if I remember correctly) and we were provided with satellite pictures as a guide to the different fields.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I started the painting later than usual so I chose to stay close to the main house on the south side of the property. To paint this I set up my easel in an open-fronted storage shed and took advantage of the shade.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Back at the studio I added a little more interest to the far distance and enhanced some of the blue color contrasts.</p>
